# The build context is an allowlist: everything is left out, and .git and
# every tracked top-level entry come back, so a build without make stamps the
# checkout's identity and git status in the build sees no deleted tracked file.
# The drops after them leave out what Git ignores inside those entries, so
# local worktrees, evidence, caches and credential files never reach the
# engine. TestTheContainerBuildContextHoldsGitAndEveryTrackedFileAlone holds
# this list to git ls-files.
*
!.git
!.agents
!.claude
!.codex
!.dockerignore
!.github
!.gitignore
!AGENTS.md
!CLAUDE.md
!Dockerfile
!Makefile
!README.md
!ansible
!api
!audits
!cmd
!docs
!e2e
!examples
!go.mod
!go.sum
!internal
!scripts
!specs
!test
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees
.codex/*
!.codex/hooks.json
!.codex/rules/bootwright.rules
examples/wip
examples/multidc-platform/secrets
examples/full-platforms/multidc-platform/secrets
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.cover
**/*.log
**/*.tmp
**/*.test
internal/controller/runtimelock/wheels/*.whl
